  "finding": "CLAIM_REFUTED: of 36 audited elements (12 ingredient choices, 12 loading levels, 12 process parameters drawn from blueprint.md Sections 1-2, cro_protocol.md, and capture_template.json), 36/36 carry NO MEASURED/MODELED/ASSUMED tag at all. The deliverable corpus's own evidence-tier vocabulary (blueprint.md line 7: REAL-ARITHMETIC / RULE-CITED / MODELED-VALIDATED / CRO-GATED) is a different, coarser, receipt-level scheme that is never applied per-ingredient or per-process-parameter in the BOM table or the process prose, and zero occurrences of the literal word 'confidence' exist anywhere in the three-file corpus. This directly instantiates the refutation criterion's first clause ('lacks a MEASURED, MODELED or ASSUMED tag with a confidence rating') for all 100% of audited elements -- the crosswalk required by CF-TIER's done_criterion does not exist yet in any form, so the second clause (MODELED/ASSUMED elements cross-referencing a resolving Dataset Ledger entry) is vacuously also unmet since no element carries a MODELED/ASSUMED tag to cross-reference from. Independently, zero of the 14 live Dataset Ledger entries declare serves.module_gaps containing 'amphora-cro-protocol-packager', so the ledger side of the crosswalk has no entries waiting to be pointed at even if the recipe side were tagged.",
  "fire_sequence": 1,
